INT. NATURAL HISTORY TAXIDERMY HALL - AFTER HOURS

Glass eyes glitter in the dark. A moth-eaten lion, a mounted heron in mid-strike, a polar bear gone the color of old teeth. The air smells of camphor and lacquer. A single green exit sign makes the room look underwater.

CURATOR AUGUSTINE FELLOWES-BAI, 60, gaunt, white gloves, an enormous ring of keys, stands before the heron with his back to the door. He talks to the bird like an old friend.

AUGUSTINE
Not tonight, old man. Tonight they're coming for us.

Heels on marble. DETECTIVE ZOFIA ARRINGTON, 40s, tailored coat, a flashlight she hasn't turned on, steps through the archway. Her eyes find him, then the dark, then him again.

ZOFIA
Mr. Fellowes-Bai.

AUGUSTINE
Detective Arrington. You are early.

ZOFIA
I'm on time. You said midnight.

AUGUSTINE
Did I? I may have meant yesterday's midnight.

He turns. His gloves are white. His hands are not quite steady.

ZOFIA
(to the room)
Whoever's behind the display cases, come out now. Slowly.

Silence. Then, from the diorama of an African savannah, a single glass eye catches the exit light and holds it.

AUGUSTINE
There's no one. Only the animals.

ZOFIA
(lower, muttering)
Every case has a rear panel. Every rear panel has a latch.

She crosses the hall, tests the nearest latch. Locked. She tries the next.

ZOFIA (CONT'D)
(to Augustine)
You said you found the first body at nine.

AUGUSTINE
At nine twenty. Under the bear.

ZOFIA
Who was it?

AUGUSTINE
A boy. Nineteen. A volunteer.

ZOFIA
Name?

AUGUSTINE
Pellam. Pellam Okonkwo. He cleaned the glass.

ZOFIA
And the bear is where?

AUGUSTINE
Behind you.

She turns. The polar bear looms in the dark, huge and patient. She switches on the flashlight. The beam finds a stain on the floor, scrubbed, but pale.

ZOFIA
Someone cleaned this.

AUGUSTINE
I did. It seemed the decent thing.

ZOFIA
Decent. Mr. Fellowes-Bai, that's called tampering.

AUGUSTINE
Is it? I thought it was called mercy.

She sweeps the beam up the bear's shoulder, along the fur, to the glass eyes.

ZOFIA
(low, to herself)
Nobody oils a taxidermy bear's joints.

AUGUSTINE
I beg your pardon?

ZOFIA
The knees. They're oiled. Look.

She steps close. The beam picks out a faint sheen, wet, along the hinge of the left hind leg.

AUGUSTINE
Maintenance.

ZOFIA
At midnight. On a stuffed bear.

AUGUSTINE
We are a very careful institution.

ZOFIA
(raising her voice, for the hall)
Whoever's inside, you have ten seconds, and then I call it in and every officer in the district comes through that door with dogs.

Silence. Then, slowly, with a click of old brass, the bear's chest opens like a cabinet.

Augustine closes his eyes.

AUGUSTINE
Ah.

ZOFIA
Mr. Fellowes-Bai. What is in the bear?

AUGUSTINE
Everything I could not bury.

ZOFIA
(to herself)
Of course it is.
